    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8su",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8st",
          "text": "The term “personal injury” covers a broad area of civil law. It refers to a range of scenarios, or claims, that arise from injuries caused to one person by another person’s or party’s negligence. The victims in personal injury claims usually seek compensation from the at-fault party’s insurance company.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8sw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sv",
          "text": "In Colorado, most personal injury lawsuits need filing within two years of the date of injury. However, there are different deadlines for different types of injury claims and negligent parties. It is always prudent to seek the advice of an experienced Highlands Ranch injury lawyer to avoid losing the right to file a lawsuit.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
